--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ETHICAL USE & RESPONSIBLE MONITORING ADDENDUM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
InfoSphere is engineered exclusively for defensive, educational, aesthetic, and
authorized personal workstation observability. By downloading, compiling, or
using this software, you agree to the following ethical principles:

1. AUTHORIZED USE ONLY: You may only monitor systems, local interfaces, and
   network equipment that you personally own or have explicit, documented
   permission to observe.
2. NO MALICIOUS OR OFFENSIVE USE: Under no circumstances may this software or its
   underlying telemetry modules be used for unauthorized network intrusion,
   packet interception, port scanning, denial-of-service, or surveillance of
   third-party devices without prior consent.
3. LOCAL PRIVACY: InfoSphere is designed with a strict privacy-first architecture.
   All hardware metrics, network states, and telemetry snapshots remain strictly
   local to your workstation and are never transmitted to external telemetry
   servers or third-party trackers.
4. COMPLIANCE WITH APPLICABLE LAWS: Users are solely responsible for ensuring
   their use of this software complies with all local, national, and international
   cybersecurity laws, regulations, and institutional Acceptable Use Policies (AUP).
